  <h3>Conclusion</h3><p>India’s role in BRICS+ expansion demonstrates its diplomatic balancing skill: asserting leadership in the Global South, leveraging economic partnerships, and keeping autonomy from both West and China. While contradictions within the bloc limit its coherence, BRICS+ signals the erosion of Western monopoly in global governance. For UPSC aspirants, this case captures how India maneuvers between principles of multipolarity and the pragmatics of national interest.</p>
